"""AQS-ELEC-007 storage and generation sizing page, written from the plant graph.

`docs-authority/_power_sizing.py` sizes the photovoltaic array, the flow battery, the inverters and
the backup generator, and `flow_graph/param/write_graph.py` power() writes the results to the graph.
This script reads them back from the graph and the drivers and writes
docs-authority/POWER_SIZING.md, so the page cannot drift from the sized values. The code basis
section is appended afterwards by flow_graph/param/code_basis.py.

Run: python3 docs-authority/_power_sizing_doc.py
"""
import json, os, sys
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); sys.path.insert(0, ROOT); os.chdir(ROOT)
from flow_graph.param import drivers as DR
from flow_graph.param import backup_fuel as BF

d = DR.load()
g = json.load(open('flow_graph/plant_flow_graph.json')); N = {n['unit_id']: n for n in g['nodes']}
P = lambda u: (N.get(u) or {}).get('params') or {}
pv, es, inv, gen = P('PV_ARRAY'), P('ZNBR2'), P('SOL_ARK_60K'), P('BACKUP_GEN')
fc = N.get('FUEL_CELL') or {}; loop = P('FUEL_CELL').get('reversible_loop') or {}
el = (g.get('mvs') or {}).get('electrical') or {}
q = lambda x: (x or {}).get('value') if isinstance(x, dict) else x
def f(v, nd=0):
    if v is None or v == '': return 'not sized'
    return f'{v:,.{nd}f}' if isinstance(v, (int, float)) else str(v)
roof = pv.get('roof') or {}; ic = inv.get('interconnection') or {}
crit = BF.critical_list(N, d); crit_kw = sum(crit.values())
import math
rule_kw = math.ceil(1.25 * crit_kw / 5) * 5; drv_kw = DR.val(d, 'backup_gen_rated_kW')
red = inv.get('redundancy') or {}
need_kw = q(el.get('need_kw')); ext_kw = q((N.get('EXT_HALL') or {}).get('continuous_kw')); rect_ew = P('RECTIFIER').get('rect_ac_input_kW')
rect_row = q((N.get('RECTIFIER') or {}).get('continuous_kw'))
s17 = next(((e.get('rate') or {}).get('value') for e in g['edges'] if e.get('from_unit_id') == 'SOL_ARK_60K' and e.get('to_unit_id') == 'RECTIFIER' and 'elec' in (e.get('layers') or [])), None)
_num = lambda *v: all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in v)
if _num(need_kw, ext_kw, rect_ew):
    parts = (f'The plant bus demand of {need_kw:.1f} kW has three parts. The extension hall `EXT_HALL` takes {ext_kw:.1f} kW (`EXT_HALL.continuous_kw`). '
             f'The rectifier input for the electrowinning cells at the bounding current is {rect_ew:.1f} kW (`RECTIFIER.params.rect_ac_input_kW`). '
             f'The remaining {need_kw - ext_kw - rect_ew:.1f} kW is the sum of the continuous loads of the other units and the feeds of the inverter bus, as `docs-authority/_power_sizing.py` adds them. '
             f'The load list AQS-ELEC-003 gives a connected load of {need_kw - rect_ew:.1f} kW, which is the bus demand less the rectifier input for the cells: it lists the cells as direct-current loads behind the rectifier and leaves them out of its alternating-current sum.')
else:
    parts = 'The parts of the plant bus demand cannot be stated because the extension hall load or the rectifier input is not on the graph.'

md = ['# Storage and generation sizing', '',
      'Document number: AQS-ELEC-007', 'Revision: H', 'Date: 2026-10-29',
      'Generated by `docs-authority/_power_sizing_doc.py` from the plant graph and `flow_graph/param/drivers.json`. Do not edit by hand; change the generator or its inputs and run `python3 -m flow_graph.param.regen`.', '',
      '| Rev | Description | Date |', '|---|---|---|',
      '| A | First issue: photovoltaic array, storage, inverters and backup generator for two electrowinning cases | 2026-10-15 |',
      '| B | Bounding case written to the graph (X-RSZ-02) | 2026-10-15 |',
      '| C | Acid and base loop loads added (X-PAR acid-loop decision) | 2026-10-15 |',
      '| D | Photovoltaic array on the roof only; the building grows until its roof carries the array (X-PAR-07) | 2026-10-15 |',
      '| E | Array at the oversize factor, storage charged on a cloudy day, inverters sized for export (X-PAR-09, decision D75) | 2026-10-15 |',
      '| F | Hall heating and cooling compared; air-source heat pumps kept (X-PAR-08, decision D77) | 2026-10-15 |',
      '| G | Generated from the graph. Revision F had become a hand-kept page whose values no longer matched the graph; the page now reports the values the sizing writes | 2026-10-29 |',
      '| H | The plant bus demand split into its parts and reconciled with the connected load of AQS-ELEC-003; the rectifier feeder checked against the rectifier input | 2026-10-29 |', '',
      '## 1. Purpose and scope', '',
      'This page reports how the plant\'s electricity is generated and stored: the photovoltaic (PV) array on the roof, the zinc-bromine flow battery `ZNBR2`, the hybrid inverters `SOL_ARK_60K`, the proton exchange membrane (PEM) fuel cell `FUEL_CELL`, the export to the grid and the standby generator `BACKUP_GEN`. It states the method and the results. The calculation is in `docs-authority/_power_sizing.py`; `flow_graph/param/write_graph.py` writes its results to the graph, and this page reads them from there. The ground-source heat pump, the organic Rankine cycle unit and the generator fuels are described in AQS-PWR-002 (`GEOTHERMAL_BACKUP.md`). Every value is a study value.', '',
      '## 2. Method', '',
      '- Demand. The plant bus demand is the converged continuous load of every unit, including the conditioned extension hall `EXT_HALL`, taken as a flat profile over the day because the process runs continuously.',
      '- Array. The balancing nameplate is the array that delivers the daily demand at the PV yield (driver `pv_yield_kWh_kWp_d`) after the system derate (`pv_system_derate`), with the night served from storage at its round-trip efficiency (`storage_round_trip`, `night_hours`). The installed array is the balancing nameplate times `pv_oversize_factor`, so that the plant has a saleable surplus. The array is on the roof only; the solver grows the building footprint on its bay grid until the roof, after fire access pathways, carries the array.',
      '- Storage. The battery carries the plant bus demand through the night (`night_hours`), so its energy is the demand times the night hours. Its charge rate is the array peak on a cloudy day less the direct load, as recorded in `ZNBR2.params.charge_basis`.',
      '- Fuel cell. The fuel cell turns stored hydrogen from the electrolyser `H2O_ELYZ` back into electricity at a set continuous output. Its round-trip efficiency, from electricity to hydrogen and back, is recorded in `FUEL_CELL.params.reversible_loop`. AQS-FC-001 (`FUEL_CELL.md`) describes it.',
      '- Inverters. The inverter count carries the array output at noon with the store full, which is when export peaks.',
      '- Backup. The generator rating is the driver `backup_gen_rated_kW`. Section 5 compares it with the rule in the driver note, which is 125 % of the critical load list rounded up to a 5 kW step on the standby basis of NFPA 110. The critical loads must be carried for `crit_autonomy_d` days without sun.', '',
      '## 3. Results', '',
      'Table 3.1 gives the sized values as the graph holds them.', '',
      'Table 3.1. Storage and generation sizing results', '',
      '| Quantity | Value | Unit | Graph field |', '|---|---|---|---|',
      f'| Plant bus demand | {f(q(el.get("need_kw")), 1)} | kW | `mvs.electrical.need_kw` |',
      f'| Mean-day average generation of the installed array | {f(q(el.get("target_kw")), 1)} | kW | `mvs.electrical.target_kw` |',
      f'| PV balancing nameplate | {f(pv.get("balance_kWp"))} | kWp | `PV_ARRAY.params.balance_kWp` |',
      f'| PV oversize factor | {f(pv.get("oversize_factor"), 1)} | - | `PV_ARRAY.params.oversize_factor` |',
      f'| PV installed nameplate | {f(pv.get("nameplate_kw"))} | kWp | `PV_ARRAY.params.nameplate_kw` |',
      f'| PV modules | {f(pv.get("count"))} | - | `PV_ARRAY.params.count` |',
      f'| PV array area | {f(pv.get("area_m2"))} | m² | `PV_ARRAY.params.area_m2` |',
      f'| Roof footprint | {f(roof.get("footprint_m2"))} | m² | `PV_ARRAY.params.roof.footprint_m2` |',
      f'| Roof capacity after pathways | {f(roof.get("roof_capacity_kWp"), 1)} | kWp | `PV_ARRAY.params.roof.roof_capacity_kWp` |',
      f'| Storage energy | {f(es.get("kWh"))} | kWh | `ZNBR2.params.kWh` |',
      f'| Storage charge rate | {f(es.get("charge_kW"))} | kW | `ZNBR2.params.charge_kW` |',
      f'| Storage discharge rate | {f(es.get("discharge_kW"))} | kW | `ZNBR2.params.discharge_kW` |',
      f'| Hybrid inverters | {f(inv.get("count"))} | - | `SOL_ARK_60K.params.count` |',
      f'| Inverter capacity | {f(inv.get("kW"))} | kW | `SOL_ARK_60K.params.kW` |',
      f'| Export at noon, store full | {f(ic.get("export_peak_kW"), 1)} | kW | `SOL_ARK_60K.params.interconnection.export_peak_kW` |',
      f'| Export energy, clear day | {f(ic.get("export_kWh_d_clear"))} | kWh/d | `SOL_ARK_60K.params.interconnection.export_kWh_d_clear` |',
      f'| Fuel cell continuous output | {f(q(fc.get("continuous_kw")), 1)} | kW | `FUEL_CELL.continuous_kw` |',
      f'| Fuel cell loop round-trip efficiency | {f(loop.get("round_trip"), 3)} | - | `FUEL_CELL.params.reversible_loop.round_trip` |',
      f'| Backup generator rating | {f(gen.get("rated_kW"))} | kW | `BACKUP_GEN.params.rated_kW` |', '',
      parts, '',
      f'Table 3.2 lists the critical loads that the backup generator carries. They total {crit_kw:.2f} kW. They come from `flow_graph/param/backup_fuel.py`, which takes them from the drivers and the graph.', '',
      'Table 3.2. Critical loads', '', '| Load | Power (kW) |', '|---|---|'] + [f'| {k} | {v:.2f} |' for k, v in crit.items()] + ['',
      '## 4. Decisions', '',
      '- The array is on the roof only. A ground-mounted field was removed, and the building grows until its roof carries the array (X-PAR-07).',
      '- The array is oversized by `pv_oversize_factor` so that the plant exports a surplus (decision D75).',
      '- The extension hall is heated and cooled by air-source heat pumps. A ground-source system was compared and gave a gain inside the uncertainty of the inputs while needing a large bore field, so the air-source design was kept (decision D77).', '',
      '## 5. Checks', '',
      (f'The rule in the driver note gives a generator rating of {rule_kw} kW for the critical loads in Table 3.2. The driver holds {f(drv_kw)} kW. ' + ('The two agree.' if abs(rule_kw - (drv_kw or 0)) < 1e-6 else 'The two differ, so either the driver or its note must be corrected; the owner decides which.')),
      '',
      (f'The bus section rating in `SOL_ARK_60K.params.redundancy` was computed for a bus demand of {f(red.get("bus_demand_kW"), 1)} kW. ' + ('This matches the plant bus demand in Table 3.1.' if abs((red.get('bus_demand_kW') or 0) - (q(el.get('need_kw')) or 0)) < 0.5 else f'The plant bus demand in Table 3.1 is {f(q(el.get("need_kw")), 1)} kW, so the section rating must be recomputed by the stage that writes it.')), '']
if _num(s17, rect_row, rect_ew) and s17 < rect_row + rect_ew - 0.05:
    md += ([] if md[-1] == '' else ['']) + [f'The rectifier is fed from the inverter bus by stream S17 at {s17:.1f} kW, which is the {rect_row:.1f} kW of its 48 V rails and auxiliaries. Its input at the bounding current is at least {rect_row + rect_ew:.1f} kW, because the input for the electrowinning cells is added in the bus demand but not in the feed. The feed and the one-line diagram AQS-ELEC-002, which uses it, must be brought to the full input by the stage that writes S17. This page does not change either value.']
open('docs-authority/POWER_SIZING.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md))
print('docs-authority/POWER_SIZING.md written')
